        // To achieve this, we set up the bad contract as the msg.sender? That is not possible. Alternative approach: we make actor be a thin forwarder that on receiving the low-level call reverts. Simpler: deploy a Forwarder that on receive attempts to call back and revert the send — but the distinguishing behavior is a failing recipient of the low-level send. So make the recipient itself revert: have actor be the bad contract and fund it before Put by having its address hold ETH and allow Put call from bad (bad must be a contract able to call Put). We'll implement Put via vm.prank to have msg.sender equal to the bad contract address and fund it.
        // For simplicity and correctness: use the deployed Reverter as the actor that both Put (we can vm.prank to have msg.sender == address(bad)) and then Collect (vm.prank(address(bad))) so that Collect will try to send to the bad contract (which reverts). First fund bad so it can call Put.

    }
